Generally looks very good.

@jukkar, myself and probably @ycsin have a few suggestions to maybe line up closer with what is already implemented so far.

The one thing that I think we're not addressing though, is that many of the `_SC_XXX` `sysconf()` queries mirror `_POSIX_XXX` constants or sometimes just straight defines ([this table](https://pubs.opengroup.org/onlinepubs/9699919799/functions/sysconf.html), for reference).

So perhaps it's better to do this:

```cpp
/* define non-underscore constants */
#define PTHREAD_KEYS_MAX                COND_CODE_1(CONFIG_PTHREAD_IPC, (CONFIG_MAX_PTHREAD_KEY_COUNT), (-1L))
/* ... */

/* define _POSIX_XXX constants */
#define _POSIX_CLOCK_SELECTION        COND_CODE_1(CONFIG_POSIX_CLOCKS, (_POSIX_VERSION), (-1L))
/* ... */

/* define sysconf() variants */
#define __z_posix_sysconf_SC_THREAD_KEYS_MAX        PTHREAD_KEYS_MAX
/* ... */
#define __z_posix_sysconf_SC_CLOCK_SELECTION        _POSIX_CLOCK_SELECTION
```

Otherwise, thank you @awojasinski for taking the time to read, understand, and implement this feature! It was on the backburner for a long time and is extremely important 😁 🥳 🙏
